From: H713 maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] h713: FEL rescue SPL re-enters FEL at EL3 after DRAM init

"sunxi-fel uboot" has never worked on H713 (docs/flash.md, "Known
gap"). The SPL returns to the BROM by eret, which leaves FEL at Secure
EL1. sunxi-fel can still move memory there, but starting BL31 needs an
RMR write, which is EL3-only.

CONFIG_H713_SPL_FEL_REENTER (default n, FEL rescue builds only) trains
DRAM and then warm-resets the core into AArch32 with both FEL flags set:
RTC GP7 for our boot0 hook (0008) and GP2 for the stock boot0. A core
reset leaves the DRAM controller alone. The BROM reloads the first stage
from LBA 0x10 at EL3, and that stage branches back into FEL before it
touches DRAM. The host then loads BL31 and U-Boot proper into the
trained DRAM and starts them with reset64.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
index 19975d26..95372163 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-sunxi/board.c
@@ -213,9 +213,60 @@ static int gpio_init(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_H713_SPL_FEL_REENTER
+#include <asm/system.h>
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+
+#define H713_RTC_GP2		0x07090108UL	/* stock boot0's efex flag */
+#define H713_RTC_GP7		0x0709011cUL	/* our boot0 hook's marker */
+#define H713_STOCK_EFEX_FLAG	0x5aa5a55a
+#define H713_FEL_MARKER		0x0fe1b007
+
+/*
+ * return_to_fel() on H713 erets into the BROM at Secure EL1, where sunxi-fel
+ * can still read and write memory but can never start BL31 or another SPL:
+ * both need RMR, which is EL3-only.  Instead, leave DRAM trained and
+ * warm-reset this core into AArch32.  A core reset does not touch the DRAM
+ * controller.  The BROM runs again at EL3 and loads the first stage from
+ * LBA 0x10; ours (boot0 hook, GP7) and the stock boot0 (GP2) both branch
+ * straight back into FEL on their flag, before touching DRAM.  The host then
+ * writes BL31 and U-Boot proper and starts them with "reset64".
+ *
+ * Both flags are set because either first stage may be installed; whichever
+ * runs clears its own, and the host clears the other.  A first stage that
+ * honours neither boots normally, so this is for FEL rescue builds only.
+ */
+static void h713_fel_reenter(void)
+{
+	if (current_el() != 3) {
+		printf("H713: not at EL3, plain FEL return\n");
+		return;
+	}
+
+	writel(H713_FEL_MARKER, H713_RTC_GP7);
+	writel(H713_STOCK_EFEX_FLAG, H713_RTC_GP2);
+	printf("H713: DRAM ready, warm reset to re-enter FEL at EL3\n");
+	udelay(2000);	/* let the UART drain */
+
+	if (dcache_status())
+		flush_dcache_all();
+
+	/* RMR_EL3: RR=1 requests the warm reset, AA64=0 resets into AArch32 */
+	asm volatile("dsb sy\n"
+		     "isb\n"
+		     "msr RMR_EL3, %0\n"
+		     "isb\n"
+		     "1: wfi\n"
+		     "b 1b\n" : : "r"(2UL) : "memory");
+}
+#endif
+
 static int spl_board_load_image(struct spl_image_info *spl_image,
 				struct spl_boot_device *bootdev)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_H713_SPL_FEL_REENTER
+	h713_fel_reenter();
+#endif
 	debug("Returning to FEL sp=%x, lr=%x\n", fel_stash.sp, fel_stash.lr);
 	return_to_fel(fel_stash.sp, fel_stash.lr);
 
diff --git a/board/sunxi/Kconfig b/board/sunxi/Kconfig
index ff5057cb..57b9fb3c 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/board/sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -33,6 +33,19 @@ config H713_SPL_FEL_MARKER
 	  to the BROM's FEL entry, still at EL3, the same way the stock boot0
 	  handles "efex".  This gives a USB recovery path that needs no button.
 
+config H713_SPL_FEL_REENTER
+	bool "H713 FEL rescue: re-enter FEL at EL3 after DRAM init"
+	depends on MACH_SUN50I_H713 && SPL
+	default n
+	help
+	  When started over FEL, train DRAM and then warm-reset the core into
+	  AArch32 with both FEL flags set (RTC GP7 for our boot0 hook, GP2 for
+	  the stock boot0), instead of returning to the BROM at EL1.  The
+	  first stage on eMMC sends the board straight back into FEL at EL3,
+	  with DRAM still trained, so the host can load BL31 and U-Boot proper
+	  and start them.  Needs a first stage that honours one of the flags.
+	  FEL rescue builds only; never enable this in a shipping image.
+
 config H713_VENDOR_CHAINLOAD
 	bool "H713: one-shot chainload of the vendor boot chain"
 	depends on MACH_SUN50I_H713
